<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! Otakiage ~ the carrier lifecycle

''A carrier that served ends in front of someone, or it does not end.'' The house names each move a governed carrier makes — pour, rule, promote, fold, burn — and gives each a who, a witness and a record, so no ending rides a spirit's memory of the last one.

The name borrows the Shinto return-rite (お焚き上げ), which //returns// a thing that served rather than discarding it, and forbids the silent drop-off: 「黙って置いていかずご相談下さい。」 — do not leave it silently; consult. The field, the house measurements and the rhymes this law rests on stand in the record (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/otakiage`>>).

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/the-lifecycle`>>

!! The lifecycle ~ stages, kinds, transitions

!!! The tag family

''The stage rides `tags`, on governed memes only.'' Five stages — `lifecycle/designed` · `lifecycle/standing` · `lifecycle/folded` · `lifecycle/harvest` · `lifecycle/retiring` — ride the mechanism TiddlyWiki already indexes, so `[tag[lifecycle/designed]]` answers in the wiki and a stage renders.

''A carrier with no `lifecycle/*` tag stands UNGOVERNED'' — law, record, reference, fiction-canon concept — and `meme check` enforces nothing on it. A missing tag MUST NOT read as a stage; it reads as //this carrier declines the ladder//, which stays cheap.

''One spelling per office.'' The tag carries the stage; `status-why` carries the witness sentence a tag cannot carry; `cacheable` instructs the API server behind the Lares, and no house code reads it. A carrier meta carries no `status` key and no `retain` key.

!!! Axis A ~ standing: the stages, in order

```
<<~ has entity=`Stage` name=`fleeting` params=`tag/none holds/nothing-on-disk ~ a turn's scratch; the temp slot never persists`>>
<<~ has entity=`Stage` name=`designed` params=`tag/lifecycle-designed holds/a-shape-argued ~ nothing enacted; status-why names what stands unbuilt`>>
<<~ has entity=`Stage` name=`standing` params=`tag/lifecycle-standing holds/a-ruling-enacted ~ status-why names the witness that proves it`>>
<<~ has entity=`Stage` name=`folded` params=`tag/lifecycle-folded holds/pointers-alone ~ every lean closed, every ruling rehomed, every inbound edge re-pointed`>>
<<~ has entity=`Stage` name=`harvest` params=`tag/lifecycle-harvest holds/materials-awaiting-a-home ~ harvest-to names the living bag; the room's emptiness is the witness`>>
<<~ has entity=`Stage` name=`retiring` params=`tag/lifecycle-retiring holds/a-last-check-in ~ welded, nothing names it, the commit explains its own ending`>>
<<~ has entity=`Stage` name=`gone` params=`tag/none holds/git-alone ~ the shelf holds nothing; the commit holds the argument`>>
```

|! stage |! the tag |! what the carrier holds |! what `status-why` reads |! what `meme check` ENFORCES |
| ''`fleeting`'' | ''none — no carrier exists'' | a turn's scratch: a `$:/temp` tiddler, a draft in the wiki island's `temp` slot (a `MemoryTiddlerStore`, `island-recipe.ts` `buildIslandRecipe`), a spirit's working note | //nothing — it never reaches a meta block// | ''nothing''. A fleeting thing that wants a check has stopped being fleeting |
| ''`designed`'' | `lifecycle/designed` | a shape argued whole against the house and the field; leans open by design | what stands ''unbuilt'', in those words | open `-> ?` leans read ''correct''. An empty `#/leans` slot reads ''wrong'': a design with no open question has either been ruled or never argued |
| ''`standing`'' | `lifecycle/standing` | a ruling enacted, or a measurement taken and held | the ''witness'': a commit sha, a named test, a measured run, or an honest partial | an open `-> ?` in `#/leans` reads ''wrong'' unless `status-why` names it held open with its blocker. A `standing` `build` carrier whose `status-why` names no witness reads ''wrong'' |
| ''`folded`'' | `lifecycle/folded` | pointers alone: each slot says where its content went | "folded to `lar:///…`, welded, nothing points here" | ''zero'' inbound `loulou`; ''zero'' open leans; every slot carrying a fold target. Any of the three failing reads ''wrong'' and the carrier stays `standing` |
| ''`harvest`'' | `lifecycle/harvest` | a room of material awaiting a reading and a home | `harvest-to` names the living bag | the sitting names a standing harvest room as a candidate |
| ''`retiring`'' | `lifecycle/retiring` | the last check-in: welded, nothing names it | the commit explains its own ending | as `folded`: zero inbound, or the sitting reads it `held` |
| ''`gone`'' | ''none — no carrier exists'' | nothing; git holds the bytes, the commit holds the argument and its trailers (rendered by `tools/changelog-render.mjs`) | //nothing// | the shelf's ''global'' check: zero dangling edges gained |

''A ROOM full of unread material reads `harvest`, never `folded`'' — folding follows the reading. ''The last check-in reads `retiring`'' — the state a reader bisecting the history lands on.

''The harvest reading meets the house's cores.'' For each rule it LIFTs, the reading asks whether a catma registry or a pattern-integrity registry already predicts it. A predicting core carries the rule; a new tell or place it lives can sharpen that core. Where no core predicts it, the reading names a candidate. A new core, or a change to a core's rule or reason, waits for the operator's word under `rule`; the reader from another context collides before findings merge (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/mu/pattern-integrity#/recursive-reading`>>).

!!! Axis B ~ kind: what counts as enactment

```
<<~ has entity=`Kind` name=`build` params=`enactment/code-plus-a-red-first-witness ~ the default; a designed build owes a test`>>
<<~ has entity=`Kind` name=`rite` params=`enactment/invocation ~ a practice convened, never built; it can never owe code`>>
<<~ has entity=`Kind` name=`reading` params=`enactment/a-measurement-dated ~ a field scout or a census; it ages rather than breaks`>>
<<~ has entity=`Kind` name=`floor` params=`enactment/an-exit ~ a talk-story floor; it closes by moʻolelo, hoike or honest suspension`>>
```

''The kind rides `tags` too'' — `kind/rite` · `kind/build` · `kind/reading` · `kind/floor`. The prefixes keep the two questions apart on one key, so a filter never guesses which it answers.

''The axes cross and answer different questions.'' `rite` × `standing` names a convened practice; `reading` × `standing` names a dated measurement, which goes ''stale'' rather than wrong and wants a re-date, never a fire; `floor` × `folded` names the class the fire governs. A ''`build`'' carrier reading `standing` with no witness reads wrong; a ''`rite`'' carrier reading `standing` with no witness reads fine, since invocation IS its witness. Fusing the axes makes one of those two rules unstatable. `talk-story`, `hoike`, both their skills and the runbooks carry `kind/rite` and stand ungoverned.

!!! The transitions ~ six rites, each with a who, a witness and a record

|! rite |! from → to |! WHO may perform it |! WITNESS (what proves it) |! RECORD (where history keeps it) |
| ''pour'' | fleeting → designed | ''any hand'' — the operator, a Lares, a tasked spirit | `lares meme normalize` then `meme check` answers canonical; `meme check --edges` gains no dangling | the commit that adds the file; `status-why` names what stands unbuilt |
| ''rule'' | designed → standing | ''the OPERATOR alone.'' A spirit MAY argue, measure and enact; it MUST NOT move its own carrier to `standing` on its own authority | the enactment's own red-first witness — the failing test quoted first, its cure, and a CONTROL; or, for a `reading`, the dated measurement | `status-why` names the witness verbatim; the CHANGELOG carries the fact |
| ''promote'' | `docs/pono/x` → `api/pono/x` | ''the kahu quorum'' — whoever holds `cap("admin", …)` on the canon bag (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/canon-boundary`>>) | the cap gate | the commit |
| ''fold'' | standing → folded | ''the spirit that closed the last open lean'' — never the carrier's own author witnessing its own fold (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/hoike`>>) | `meme check --edges <carrier> $(git ls-files 'bags/*.mem')` shows ''zero inbound'', and a grep of the source tree and the CHANGELOG finds no `lar:` URI naming it; every ruling reachable at its new `standing` home | each slot rewritten to "folded to `lar:///…`"; `status-why` names the targets; the CHANGELOG names the fold |
| ''otakiage'' | folded → gone | ''the operator CALLS it; any hand MAY carry it'' (#/the-fire) | the fold's weld still holds at the moment of the fire (re-run, never trusted from the fold commit); the house's checks green in the same commit | the last check-in commit, then the delete commit; ''git holds the argument'', the CHANGELOG holds the fact |
| ''tombstone'' | //orthogonal — a live record leaving a live group// | `removeMeme` through any skin (`place-meme.ts`) or a person's `lares shore remove` answer (`commands/shore.ts`) | a vanished disk file stays pending; a person answers by name, or a signed standing instruction covers its bounded class (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/api/disk-projection#/projection-law`>>) | the synced tree's `null` (`synced-tree.ts`); the group's whole tombstone set in the result |

''The two-commit shape.'' The last check-in and the delete ride ''separate commits'', so the shelf carries one state in which the carrier stands complete, marked as ending, with every pointer re-aimed. A reader bisecting the history lands on a carrier that explains its own ending, never on a diff that removes it.

!!! The siblings ~ standings a carrier holds OUTSIDE the ladder

# ''`kapu` — sealed, referee-side, never ended by another hand.'' No hand but the grant-holder's ends a kapu carrier, and a sweep that cannot read a carrier MUST NOT propose it (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/kapu`>>; the grace table holds a VEIL blob eight rolls against PUBLIC's one, `cas-caps.ts` `GRACE_RATIO_BY_TIER`).
# ''`tombstone` — a record removed inside a live group.'' The lifecycle governs a carrier's standing in the shelf; the tombstone governs a record's presence in a group (`removeMeme` takes the whole group; `tombstoneInBag` hides where `removeInBag` removes; `pairRenames` declines ambiguous matches). The two MUST NOT fuse, or a sync flake could burn a carrier.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/the-fire`>>

!! The fire ~ what burns, what never burns, who calls it

!!! What burns

''One class only:'' a carrier reading ''`folded`'' (or `retiring`, its last check-in) — every lean closed, every ruling rehomed to a `standing` address, every inbound `loulou` re-pointed, `meme check --edges` showing zero inbound — whose continued presence adds nothing a reader cannot reach at the fold target. A harvest room burns once its reading has lifted every claim that stands nowhere else.

''Nothing else.'' A carrier that went quiet does not qualify, nor one that reads stale, wrong or embarrassing. ''A wrong carrier gets corrected; a stale reading gets re-dated; an embarrassing one stays.''

!!! The rite, walked

# ''READ every file before deciding anything.'' A decision to burn rests on evidence that nothing is lost: the row names the living carrier, or the file does not burn.
# ''LIFT what stands nowhere else,'' each into a carrier that holds the surrounding law and lacks exactly that piece. A lift that lands where nothing surrounds it reads as a move, not a fold.
# ''WELD every inbound edge, before the fire and never after.'' An edge whose target nothing inherited re-aims at the carrier that RECORDS where the material went.
# ''BURN in groups, each with its own commit and its own gratitude line.'' A wave shows its shape; one commit deleting a room records nothing a reader can walk backwards.
# ''The room's declaration goes last,'' and its emptiness stands as the witness.

''A rite that ends a thing leaves the instruments reading MORE, never less:'' an exemption a gate carries for a room leaves with the room.

!!! What NEVER burns

# ''Canon under `api/pono/`.'' An address there has readers the house cannot enumerate; <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/meme#/retirement`>> governs the name, and the bytes at a canon address stay.
# ''Anything a standing `loulou` still names.'' `meme check --edges` answers it mechanically. ''The weld comes first and the fire second, always.''
# ''Anything under kapu, or sealed above the reader's tier.'' A sweep that cannot read a carrier cannot judge it.
# ''The change record.'' Commit trailers and archive tags hold the record the fire depends on; no burn rewrites history or drops a tag.
# ''Genesis.'' `node-cas.ts` `CasSweepOptions.protect` and `casSweep` refuse to sweep the genesis manifest's blobs; the same refusal rides up to the carrier layer.
# ''A carrier that authors its own permanence'', until the operator's word unsays it.
# ''Any floor with an open lean.'' An unresolved argument holds a claim on the shelf that no tidiness outranks.
# ''Anything a hoike contests.'' Burning the record a dissent hangs on would close its re-entry key by deletion.

''The hard floor:'' ''the fire burns a path, never a pattern.'' An otakiage touches one path in one tree and reaches no copy anywhere; nothing here MAY reach a record on another vessel — that plane belongs to `removeMeme` and its grace, under the caps, and the two MUST NOT meet.

''The wiki plane carries its own path.'' A tiddler — a whole meme or an ahu slot, each addressed by its full title — in one layer of one vessel's wiki stands as that wiki's path. Fire on that tiddler reaches no other layer or vessel and never meets `removeMeme`. The same ladder, READ → LIFT → WELD → BURN in groups with the declaration last, never-burn list, caller, gratitude line and two-commit shape govern it. Its doors read `lares tiddler delete <title> --recipe <r> --if-match <hash>` (`--family` for a meme root); an ahu slot leaves through a family put without that slot. A line never burns alone: a backward line inside a standing meme gets trued by an edit under the evergreen rule (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/ever-speaking-present`>>). The stage reading and its limits stand in the record (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/otakiage#/the-stage-ash`>>).

''Stage road reading, without tag migration:'' `road/state/open` reads `designed`; `road/state/landed` reads `standing`; routed, lifted and welded material reads `folded`. The standing order “o-takiage at every land” supplies the authored ending that counts as a call already made for landed road memes; proof, weld and the two commits still govern each burn.

!!! Who calls it

''The operator calls; any hand may carry.'' A Nexus lives on traffic, so its silence ends it with no admin act (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/kahu#/nexus-lifecycle`>>); a `.mem` file at a fixed path never goes quiet, and a stale carrier reads exactly like a standing one. ''The capability answers NONE where quiet does the work, and answers OPERATOR where quiet does nothing.''

A spirit MAY close a lean, run the weld and prepare the fold whole; it MUST NOT rule that the argument has ended, for the reason it may not witness its own block. ''An authored ending, ruled at pour time,'' stands as a call already made — the one shape that skips a fresh call. Judgement sits with the operator; mechanics sit with whoever runs the commands. What the carrier MUST NOT do is end in silence, and the two-commit shape enforces that.

!!! How it convenes ~ never a calendar

# ''The reading names candidates; it never burns.'' `lares meme sitting` (and `meme check --sitting`) holds the whole shelf at once and names every candidate — `lifecycle/folded` or `lifecycle/retiring` with nothing naming it, plus every harvest room still standing — then stops. ''A carrier any other carrier still names reads `held`, however its stage reads.'' The reading never exits non-zero, so a hook can run it.
# ''The operator calls the season'' — one sitting, several carriers at once, at a moment the operator names: a phase boundary, a founding, a release. A wave shows its own shape.
# ''No sigil opens the sitting;'' it convenes as a talk-story floor, which carries the three exits it needs (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/talk-story`>>).

!!! The gratitude line

The last check-in commit's body says four things and stops:

# ''What the carrier carried'' — in the present tense, as the thing it held.
# ''Where each part went'' — the fold targets by `lar:` URI, one hop to the content.
# ''What proves nothing dangles'' — the weld, re-run, quoted: the edge count and the check line.
# ''The thanks'' — one clause, in the house's own voice, naming what the carrier did.

The ending belongs to the thing's completion, never to its worthlessness — 「感謝の気持ちをこめて納める」. The subject follows the house's convention, `lar:///w1.w2.w3 — summary`, with the three-term root naming what the ending DID.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/sigils`>>

!! Sigils ~ the record inside a sitting

The sitting convenes as a talk-story floor (#/the-fire); no sigil opens it. These calls record its reading and acts. `mu` and `aperture` optionally name the seed's attention instruments (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/noosphere-boot#/mu-five-tools`>>, <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/noosphere-boot#/aperture`>>). An `unchecked` value exposes a check the call has yet to carry.

```memetic-wikitext
\procedure ~sitting(candidates never:"unchecked" held:"unchecked" mu:"00" aperture:"18/theme") Sitting (<<mu>>, <<aperture>>): candidates <<candidates>>; never burns <<never>>; held <<held>>.
\procedure ~lift(item core action:"candidate" mu:"!0" aperture:"6/beat") Lift <<item>> toward <<core>> (<<mu>>, <<aperture>>): <<action>>.
\procedure ~weld(source inbound:"unchecked" backlinks:"unchecked" search:"unchecked" owed:"unchecked" mu:"?0" aperture:"14/arc") Weld <<source>> (<<mu>>, <<aperture>>): inbound <<inbound>>; `backlinks[]` <<backlinks>>; `search[]` for bare `lar:` cites <<search>>; owed items <<owed>>.
\procedure ~burn(target proof hash:"unchecked" base:"unchecked" layers:"unchecked" commits:"unchecked" carried:"unchecked" homes:"unchecked" clear:"unchecked" thanks:"unchecked" mu:"_!" aperture:"2/pulse") Burn <<target>> (<<mu>>, <<aperture>>): proof <<proof>>; hash <<hash>> or base <<base>>; layers <<layers>>; two commits <<commits>>. Gratitude: carried <<carried>>; each part went <<homes>>; nothing dangles <<clear>>; thanks <<thanks>>.
```

`action` reads `carried` · `tell` · `lives` · `draft` · `candidate`. A `burn` target names a whole meme or an ahu slot by full title; `proof` carries no default and must name the source's completed work. A meme root carries a plain-read `hash`; an ahu family put carries its family-read `base`. `commits` names the last check-in and the burn commit; the four gratitude values form the last check-in body.

```memetic-wikitext
<<~ sitting candidates=`road/one-door` never=`canon; kapu; contested floors` held=`road/open-lean`>>
<<~ lift item=`one-door rule` core=`catma registry` action=`carried`>>
<<~ weld source=`road/one-door` inbound=`zero after repointing` backlinks=`zero` search=`zero bare cites` owed=`each item reads at its new home`>>
<<~ burn target=`lar:///example.road.folds/one-door` proof=`merged cure and read-back` hash=`sha256-…` layers=`working only` commits=`last check-in; burn` carried=`the one-door rule` homes=`lar:///example.rule.stands/one-door` clear=`zero inbound; edge check green` thanks=`you gave the rule its first path`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/rulings`>>

!! Rulings

# Operator ruling 2026-09-12: the lifecycle rides a tag family on governed memes only; `status` and `retain` leave the meta; `cacheable` stays as an API-server instruction; `lares-history` serves as the harvest room, emptied and deleted; the fire is called, never scheduled. The ruling stands verbatim, with its enactment and the walked room, at <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/otakiage#/the-lifecycle`>>.
# Operator ruling 2026-11-21 (the ever-speaking present): the law lifts from the docs record to this api meme; the record keeps the field, the house measurements, the rhymes, the examples, the leans and the questions (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/ever-speaking-present`>>).

<<~/ahu>>

